            <ArticleTitle>[Organically induced potency disorders (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>543-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The man who feels his sexual function is disturbed is at first not prepared to look for psychic grounds for the condition he considers a defect. He rather expects his physician to find an organic lesion. The knowledge of the many congenital and acquired diseases which can have a negative effect on potency permit the application of a suitable laboratory program in addition to the specific history and physical examination. If a relevant disease should be found, this must first be treated before the psychic fixation which is sure to have developed is gone into. On the other hand, should an organic disease be overlooked, even the best psychotherapy will be unsuccessful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
